<title>SWEDEN: Incentive says to dispose of Hagglunds.</title>
<headline>Incentive says to dispose of Hagglunds.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish investment and medical technology group Incentive said on Thursday that its operation Hagglunds Vehicle was not in the company's priority area and will be disposed of.</p>
<p>&quot;Hagglunds Vehicle is an excellent company with good orders and a stable operating development but this operation lies in an area that is not a priority for us, the defence industry,&quot; managing director Mikael Lilius wrote in the company's annual report.</p>
<p>&quot;Hagglunds Vehicle is a company that in the longrun will be disposed of.&quot;</p>
<p>Incentive on Thursday also announced it was selling subsidiary TA Hydronics to Britain's IMI Plc as part of its concentration on operations that can generate significant growth in value.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
